Package: dotlinplot
Title: Faithful Plots of Zero-Inflated Single-Cell Expression
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Wajid", "Iqbal", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "121088089+Wajidiqbal1@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Dotlin plots show zero-inflated distributions, such as
    single-cell gene expression, faithfully by separating two pieces of
    information: the proportion of cells in which a gene is detected, drawn as
    a bar below zero, and the distribution of the non-zero values, drawn as a
    violin with jittered points. Works with 'Seurat' and
    'SingleCellExperiment' objects and with plain data frames.
